msgid "Tuning Process Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:8
#: 5433eda33c9347bda6359b78f1cfae10
msgid "Setting the aircraft up to be ready for tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:10
#: 8892cea1d2f143f38747224831f63cec
msgid "The following parameters should be set correctly based on the specifications of your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:13
#: 4728c28db1dd46f2a1876e7327d913a6
msgid "Step 1: Battery and expo settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:15
#: b0f9e78b60674bc3b59979d92a0b6712
msgid "It is very important to ensure that the thrust curve of your VTOL motors is as linear as possible. A linear thrust curve means that changes in the actual thrust produced by a motor is directly proportional to the thrust being demanded by ArduPilot. If your thrust curve is badly non-linear then you will never produce a good tune, and in some cases may end up with such a bad tune that your vehicle can become completely unstable and crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:23
#: c2b29425d6c54f2f8db0e0e4ebcbbcc9
msgid "There are 3 common causes of a non-linear thrust curve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:25
#: b7991ce7e63744e698fc294a8c91dbcf
msgid "voltage sag as throttle is increased or the forward motor is engaged. This is very common in QuadPlanes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:26
#: 686ada30b07d4065a93e5869c2c56d72
msgid "incorrect end-point setup in the PWM range you use to your ESCs (see \"Motors setup\" below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:27
#: 347babc67e9d48799c0ff61bef346047
msgid "non-linearity in the thrust produced by your propeller, ESC and motor combination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:29
#: 41cf4042fd3e4a4c813645f7f6d53dd9
msgid "Start with setting up the voltage range to cope with voltage sag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:31
#: 048e55a6a86f492ebbf346f6360e6515
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_IDX <Q_M_BAT_IDX>`: index of the battery to use for voltage measurements on VTOL power system. Zero is the first battery, one for 2nd battery etc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:32
#: 7b66a58f6e5c4385b79f158ca0300cdd
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX <Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX>`: 4.2v x No. Cells for LiPo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:33
#: 9c96c2664cae4d3d90c41f759e370f0b
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN <Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>`: 3.3v x No. Cells for LiPo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:34
#: c95d0f1f982547f19c5c3d6997cb446c
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_OPTIONS<Q_M_OPTIONS>` = 0 (default). The default is to use sag compensated voltage for the above and during tuning computations. It can be set to 1 to use raw voltage instead of sag compensated voltage, which may improve tuning results for light vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:36
#: 87133cb714c9405cb6907cb603d8ba76
msgid "Note that :ref:`Q_M_BAT_IDX <Q_M_BAT_IDX>` needs to be for the correct battery for your VTOL motors. If you have a separate battery for forward motors and VTOL motors then make sure you use the right one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:40
#: 1ba8d15c036c4faca19833afade913e6
msgid "Next setup the thrust expo. If you are setting up a professional aircraft then you should invest in a thrust stand so you can accurately measure the true thrust for your motor/ESC/propeller combination as you vary the throttle. Then you will adjust the expo value along with the endpoints (given by motors setup below) so that the thrust between the endpoints is as linear as possible. Do not trust manufacturer data for the thrust curve as they are frequently inaccurate. See :ref:`motor-thrust-scaling` for details on thrust scaling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:48
#: fd8b625b4cf94abd9687baa5760503f6
msgid "If you are setting up a hobby grade vehicle then you can use the graph below to estimate the correct :ref:`Q_M_THST_EXPO <Q_M_THST_EXPO>` value for your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:51
#: d9d1245af8944ceebed3ee3ded446a0c
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_THST_EXPO <Q_M_THST_EXPO>`: 0.55 for 5 inch props, 0.65 for 10 inch props, 0.75 for 20 inch props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:57
#: 87a6a13c44fe437ca25df127d8092f6c
msgid "Step 2: Motors setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:59
#: c0d062d11f934b6c8d1b03fb7df8efd8
msgid "The motor parameters define the PWM output range sent to the ESCs. This is critical to ensure that the entire range of throttle values used in flight is within the linear range of your propulsion system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:64
#: 7ce1e8c552a445499976fa2dd7cb4ea6
msgid "For standard PWM based ESCs you should adjust :ref:`Q_M_PWM_MIN <Q_M_PWM_MIN>` until it is approximately 20 microseconds below the minimum value that causes the motors to just start spinning. If you are using digital motor outputs (such as DShot) then this is not necessary and the default of 1000 should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:70
#: 693073c1c2fe4d01b0495f35bfb61e8f
msgid "You should then adjust :ref:`Q_M_PWM_MAX <Q_M_PWM_MAX>` to the value where the ESCs stop producing more thrust. Note that this is commonly a bit below the default maximum of 2000. To find the value you should test with propellers removed, and use the motor test facility of your GCS to find the lowest PWM value which produces the motors maximum RPM. You should be able to tell at what PWM the motors stop producing more thrust by listening to the sound made at different PWM values, or you can use a tachometer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:79
#: 5fda6adfddb4456e9a049def8f410bf1
msgid "The :ref:`Q_M_SPIN_MIN <Q_M_SPIN_MIN>` and :ref:`Q_M_SPIN_MAX<Q_M_SPIN_MAX>` values are used to select a sub-range of the outputs to your motors which is linear. For hobby users the defaults are usually good, but for professional vehicles you should use the thrust stand data to determine the right range to produce linear thrust after the expo is applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:85
#: e7d57cf674ad4b3db234880242dd6597
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_PWM_MAX <Q_M_PWM_MAX>`: Check ESC manual for fixed range or 2000us"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:86
#: e4f6bd3f670d4b9da5eb676660319ac6
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_PWM_MIN <Q_M_PWM_MIN>`: Check ESC manual for fixed range or 1000us"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:87
#: 5bd80c741ea943a5aee5339487378a46
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_SPIN_ARM <Q_M_SPIN_ARM>`: use the :ref:`motor test feature <connect-escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:88
#: 618243b14d804497a12d90feca8df66f
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_SPIN_MAX <Q_M_SPIN_MAX>`: 0.95"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:89
#: 71a25c5df01c41a59fb6ac48241d1178
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_SPIN_MIN <Q_M_SPIN_MIN>`: use the :ref:`motor test feature <connect-escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:90
#: a92a6b11af6f4c64aa9ddfead6b133a0
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER <Q_M_THST_HOVER>`: 0.25, or below the expected hover thrust percentage (low is safe)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:93
#: 71d42613dccd47dfa4e87e7bba70853b
msgid "Step 3: PID Controller Initial Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:95
#: 00112a0bbb474daf9bbc22f573bdea33
msgid "The settings below are meant to get your PID controller acceleration and filter settings into the right approximate range for your vehicle. These parameters are critical to the tuning process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:99
#: ab000f7b6843408d9a040b235ff1bc92
msgid ":ref:`INS_ACCEL_FILTER <INS_ACCEL_FILTER>`:  10Hz to 20Hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:100
#: bf27afa9a51f48c3a955692a74531e5b
msgid ":ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>`: 80Hz for 5 inch props, 40Hz for 10 inch props, 20Hz for 20 inch props"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:101
#: 983444399d5c4998a02118e3b4e9b423
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_ACC_P_MAX<Q_A_ACC_P_MAX>`: 1100 for 10 inch props, 500 for 20 inch props, 200 for 30 inch props"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:102
#: b05f7b65ace74d3f8f83d3c680ba8fa4
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_ACC_R_MAX<Q_A_ACC_R_MAX>`: 1100 for 10 inch props, 500 for 20 inch props, 200 for 30 inch props"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:103
#: ffcf07074ef74326995eb9d85a8e53be
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX<Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX>`: 75 for 6 inch props, 67.5 for 10 inch props, 45 for 20 inch props, 22.5 for 30 inch props"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:104
#: 1a875bc3d62e4b6f9d3983b6af9732f3
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_YAW_P <Q_A_RAT_YAW_P>`: 0.5 x :ref:`Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX<Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX>` / 45"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:107
#: 31126d00bed349358944870703f41344
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_FLTD <Q_A_RAT_PIT_FLTD>`: :ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>` / 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:108
#: f03bc21d1d7a4c6db9e51e78b116e192
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_FLTT <Q_A_RAT_PIT_FLTT>`: :ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>` / 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:109
#: 67417c233d1247dd98aed2a80b17d657
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_FLTD <Q_A_RAT_RLL_FLTD>`: :ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>` / 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:110
#: cdc4fc8cac984e0c8ebe7df2ca122b0f
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_FLTT <Q_A_RAT_RLL_FLTT>`: :ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>` / 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:111
#: 9f7a14aad8ca474ba3e7d3ee796fbb86
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_YAW_FLTE <Q_A_RAT_YAW_FLTE>`: 0 for vectored yaw; 2.5 for other types of QuadPlanes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:112
#: 9cd4fb2f62f340adb484a96782dcf82f
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_YAW_FLTT <Q_A_RAT_YAW_FLTT>`: :ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>` / 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:125
#: b6c2929f7af94c8a820f2b08bd60ed11
msgid "The initial tune of the aircraft should be done **in the aircraft's most agile configuration**. This generally means that the aircraft will be at its minimum take off weight with fully charged batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:128
#: 10ad2929c5844c22999f088902f698ad
msgid "Step 4: Pilot's preparation for first flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:130
#: ea72aa91a5c741e5b4c10cdc06da5685
msgid "The first takeoff of an untuned VTOL vehicle is the most dangerous seconds of the aircraft’s life. This is where the aircraft could be very unstable causing a sudden increase in power when then results in the aircraft jumping into the air, or it may be so poorly tuned that you have insufficient control over the aircraft once it is airborne. The pilot should be extremely diligent during the tuning flights to avoid a situation that could result in injury or damage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:132
#: 457c79e18c924a30a850c821f9585b49
msgid "There are several things that the pilot can do to minimize the risk during the early tuning process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:134
#: 750b970d99b345ebb9e3873b154e7445
msgid "The pilot should conduct a motor number and orientation check (see :ref:`Checking the motor numbering with the Mission Planner Motor test <connect-escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions>`). Care should be taken to ensure that the correct frame type is selected. Incorrect frame type can result in a very fast yaw rotation or complete loss of control. Take note of the output percentage required to spin the propellers and ensure that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:136
#: e042118c6f0d44bc8e93b358dcf25949
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_SPIN_ARM <Q_M_SPIN_ARM>` is set high enough to spin the motors cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:137
#: fd84ae88f3194d5995f6a1be215e76c0
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_SPIN_MIN <Q_M_SPIN_MIN>` is set high enough to spin the motors with a minimal level of thrust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:139
#: 94d68840739f4f408c2d0acc051d3a17
msgid "All flights after a significant tuning change should be done in QSTABILIZE. QSTABIILIZE provides the pilot with significantly more control over the aircraft in the event that the attitude controllers are unstable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:140
#: 1022652e842d4836907f3b83c01e205f
msgid "The pilot should not take off in QHOVER until the altitude controller has been tested in flight. This should be done by taking off in QSTABILIZE and switching to QHOVER. Although QHOVER is rarely a problem unless the aircraft has a very low hover throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:141
#: 351325ab260645e58c7f0807d45ff809
msgid "For the initial flights the pilot should ensure that these parameters are set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:143
#: 56d9ae41fb7b43a58c599364eeb77525
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_THR_MIX_MAN <Q_A_THR_MIX_MAN>` to 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:144
#: 026a4cdcd1c74d5c8e89cd5355bd6c94
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER <Q_M_THST_HOVER>` to 0.25 (or lower than the expected hover throttle)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:146
#: 7ad3226b81a84ec19de3ef433570fdcc
msgid "Use a radio and calibrate the radio correctly (see :ref:`common-radio-control-calibration`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:147
#: a006f4f8fa0a4308a7fd93935c23af3e
msgid "Configure an ARM/DISARM switch and test it (see :ref:`Auxiliary Functions <common-auxiliary-functions>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:148
#: 8aa7a3cc73154001aaad034a82703964
msgid "Do tuning flights in low-wind condition and normal weather (no rain and between 15°C/59°F and 25°C/77°F)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:149
#: a20a3d3f7b574996b5b354dbc4a78893
msgid "Practice QSTABILIZE flight in simulator or on a low-end drone first. You should be confident to be able to takeoff and land with your untuned aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:152
#: 347b64b4adfd4867afe0e12a9a9d2707
msgid "Tuning Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:155
#: 9ddc72d49b4745d9b7c2fac5a5aa2215
msgid "Step 5: First Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:157
#: 35d5965cfcbd40efaf52fbb824fb9710
msgid "The first take off is the most dangerous time for any QuadPlane. Care must be taken to ensure the aircraft is not destroyed in the first seconds of flight and nobody is injured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:159
#: 43970c4b7d6149e7bb3474187b87d766
msgid "**Ensure that all spectators are at a safe distance**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:160
#: 8e2d3089cd8543c6887fc270c8a3f4b4
msgid "**Ensure the pilot is at a safe distance and position**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:161
#: e601478e8bc34083b02cb209052703e7
msgid "The pilot should refresh themselves on the method used to disarm the aircraft (using :ref:`Auxiliary Functions <common-auxiliary-functions>` for Motor Interlock or Arm/Disarm may be beneficial)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:163
#: 815180dfe28e472bb3c3b15ecc3f601f
msgid "This flight will allow to setup your aircraft in a \"flyable for tuning\" state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:165
#: e45ee623cdb34939971677c5793ed21d
msgid "Ensure the aircraft is in QSTABILIZE mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:166
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:168
#: 7f2dc58ced044731b7ef9a94a4482015
#: 1f50bc0ea8594186820f1a7ace4766a7
msgid "Arm the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:167
#: 256dc9e8f62b4232ba131fdca4cb360f
msgid "Immediately disarm the aircraft to ensure your disarm procedure is correct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:169
#: ee594c72327f42658e0057e49abb88d4
msgid "Slowly increase the throttle looking for signs of oscillation. (long or flexible landing gear may cause some landing gear oscillation that will only go away after the aircraft leaves the ground)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:170
#: d805b9bf8346466995eda5aa07290402
msgid "As soon as the aircraft lifts off the ground immediately put the aircraft back down as gently as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:171
#: c2a44f4eba954d60bd08c1603848af53
msgid "Disarm the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:172
#: e48dea6d19134938b377741cbdee7ab2
msgid "Evaluate what you observed to decide if you need to make adjustments to the tuning parameters or if it is safe to take off again"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:173
#: 53e75101a82a4c4689d7b71f43c49e5e
msgid "Arm and increase the throttle to initiate a takeoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:174
#: 0dab621b596648aeabf24c084fed660e
msgid "Hover at approximately 1m altitude and apply small (5 degrees) control inputs into roll and pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:175
#: faa2384542f34904a230116d0e15306d
msgid "Immediately land if any oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:177
#: 510f05fb8afd4360a9c8bdc250f6611a
msgid "Next section will explain how to remove the oscillations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:180
#: 3560701ba2714d57a28ab382bdf59b7c
msgid "Step 6: Initial aircraft tune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:182
#: 466c751ab287494e9699a3c960b104c4
msgid "The first priority when tuning a QuadPlane is to establish a stable tune, free of oscillations, that can be used to do further tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:184
#: bcd7b8259fd54b7281e4931c6bacd84a
msgid "Arm the aircraft in QSTABILIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:185
#: e1c4f20282a3441795ae24f1cd6b897d
msgid "Increase the throttle slowly until the aircraft leaves the ground"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:186
#: 60b66193aa4b4774bda6238303179c81
msgid "If the aircraft starts to oscillate immediately abort the takeoff and/or land the aircraft, and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:187
#: 002b043204544b12ba35bc94291e43e9
msgid "Reduce all the following parameters by 50%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:189
#: eb79a05016b34caea95b47a46f4d4845
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_P <Q_A_RAT_PIT_P>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:190
#: 6088bf7b1e2e43d0879e79b105d637d6
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_I <Q_A_RAT_PIT_I>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:191
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:319
#: 6e6aed2fd829424f988478fdaae97ab3
#: 617bc491bc134ea19719e88ca4ee37df
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_D <Q_A_RAT_PIT_D>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:192
#: c3898933939645b5bf2f2d8d9748be61
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_P <Q_A_RAT_RLL_P>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:193
#: 3a126c39d1c3440382ab7a7dfc613250
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_I <Q_A_RAT_RLL_I>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:194
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:317
#: 98480fab608a4bcca773eacebdf55925
#: 631659a801964ba68b890eac8e38a8d1
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_D <Q_A_RAT_RLL_D>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:196
#: 3d4cba163a4f4e8f90b9853a04b2a80f
msgid "This process is repeated until the aircraft can hover without oscillations being detectable visually or audibly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:198
#: b4fa4efa56394e66b978d90751366d2a
msgid "If the aircraft has very long or flexible landing gear then you may need to leave the ground before ground resonance stops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:200
#: f2d42fed550043c4b2d2e0057d0cbec0
msgid "Be aware that in this state the aircraft may be very slow to respond to large control inputs and disturbances. The pilot should be extremely careful to put minimal stick inputs into the aircraft to avoid the possibility of a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:203
#: 8fc22df4cfb349a78504bf93f7337d74
msgid "Step 7: Test QHOVER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:205
#: 15b0f60e21024392b2c187943b53d2c4
msgid "This test will allow to test the altitude controller and ensure the stability of your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:207
#: c3d25e8c17bc4284a547e820ed4170a9
msgid "Check :ref:`Q_M_HOVER_LEARN <Q_M_HOVER_LEARN>` is set to 2. This will allow the controller to learn by itself the correct hover value when flying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:209
#: 27455a5adf18436ab0e487c6f0c95608
msgid "the Hover throttle value is only \"learned\" when the attitude is not being commanded by the pilot, or autopilot (ie QLOITER,etc.), to exceed 5 degrees from neutral for two seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:211
#: 54a4944dd1184093a9318f19ac364676
msgid "Take off in QSTABILIZE and increase altitude to 5m. Switch to QHOVER and be ready to switch back to QSTABILIZE. If the aircraft is hovering at a very low hover throttle value you may hear a reasonably fast oscillation in the motors. Ensure the aircraft has spent at least 30 seconds in hover to let the hover throttle parameter converge to the correct value. Land and disarm the aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:213
#: 1528e89276d041818a0a0711682d20fd
msgid "Set these parameters on ground and preferably disarm  (A confident pilot could set them in flight with GCS):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:215
#: 4df72cc92e0544e68f6392be4838a34f
msgid ":ref:`Q_P_D_ACC_I<Q_P_D_ACC_I>` to 0.2 x :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER <Q_M_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:216
#: 58983a2b79a1457b83fa03b24b471f20
msgid ":ref:`Q_P_D_ACC_P<Q_P_D_ACC_P>` to 0.1 x :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER <Q_M_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:218
#: 31e8c915871f46098125190bffbd558c
msgid "In Plane 4.6 and earlier these parameters were named ``Q_P_ACCZ_I`` and ``Q_P_ACCZ_P`` and were scaled 10x larger:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:220
#: 7d59ba768873421a81336128bcf9dcae
msgid "``Q_P_ACCZ_I`` to 2 x :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER <Q_M_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:221
#: 22896b43158d430cbf3e9dcc052c8cf9
msgid "``Q_P_ACCZ_P`` to :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER <Q_M_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:223
#: a108d06bdf40446fbb1c6fd8f3ee785b
msgid "If the QuadPlane in QHOVER starts to move up and down, the vertical position and velocity controllers may need to be reduced by 50%. These values are: :ref:`Q_P_D_POS_P<Q_P_D_POS_P>` and :ref:`Q_P_D_VEL_P<Q_P_D_VEL_P>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:225
#: 16710138e6a4428cb1a8c82d3fe3a0c8
msgid "If the :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER<Q_M_THST_HOVER>` learned should be ~0.3-0.6. Higher values indicate that insufficient thrust is available, either due to motor system design, obstructed prop air flow by the fuselage or wings, or excessive yaw bias (see next section)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:228
#: 075014692cae489bbafbcdced45d4c6d
msgid "Step 8: Yaw Bias"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:230
#: f5330e03287e46cb957cc2b2834f67c7
msgid "A common problem in QuadPlanes is excessive amount of VTOL power being used to maintain yaw hold instead of providing lift. This can be caused by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:233
#: ca3a760dc70d469d88bf77f5b418ffb7
msgid "small misalignment of the VTOL motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:234
#: 2792124bf8cb4ae2ba37fa0af38c014a
msgid "frame twist (often caused by wing twist) as thrust is applied"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:235
#: 8546d4e3aab4458ea0b334c95a5c1ca7
msgid "obstructed prop air flow by wings in :ref:`TVBS type tailsitters<tvbs>` making vectored yaw by motor tilt less effective. This can also cause enough reduction in normal thrust to make hovering and VTOL climb difficult."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:237
#: 713390831acd4169b4f57f2ae88e9cdc
msgid "If too much power is needed to maintain yaw then the aircraft could lose yaw control during transitions, or could lose roll and pitch stability. The most common symptom is a high hover throttle point, or even the inability to rise into a hover at high throttle stick position. For larger QuadPlanes it is common to need to deliberately tilt the motors by a couple of degrees to increase yaw authority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:242
#: 7e1cb7d4876b449b8c8c015e3810d84b
msgid "for an X frame type (:ref:`Q_FRAME_TYPE<Q_FRAME_TYPE>` = 1), the motors should be tilted outwards. For an H frame (:ref:`Q_FRAME_TYPE<Q_FRAME_TYPE>` = 3) they should be tilted inwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:246
#: d5a0476750e94e54be6ddf986f65ec8d
msgid "You should check the amount of thrust being used to maintain yaw by looking at the RATE YOut value in your hover logs. If it is over 10% (a value of 0.1) when hovering in no wind with no pilot input,then you have a problem with yaw asymmetry that should be fixed. Just hovering in place may look fine and you may not see the problem until you examine the log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:252
#: c0af2f5683484ca39158a79761fbc0d0
msgid "The log below shows RATE.YOut (orange) increasing dramatically while motor 1 (RCOUT.C5) is idling and motor 2 (RCOUT.C6) is barely working, but at the same time motor 3 (RCOUT.C7) and motor 4 (RCOUT.C8) are are running > 50% output. This limits how much higher the firmware could raise the overall thrust due to these motors maxing out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:259
#: 91ae1d5e7c914b78904ef8de6ef4abfb
msgid "Fixing yaw asymmetry can involve mechanical improvements such as stiffening the airframe to resist twisting, making sure prop flow is unobstructed by the wings on TVBS frames,or correcting/adjusting motor tilt angles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:262
#: afacdc2a108149fb9d67801a5b6699d2
msgid "Some QuadPlanes will benefit from being setup as H frames instead of X frames. Which works best depends on the way the motor mounts twist when under thrust. If you have a persistent problem with yaw control then consider trying to change the frame type between X and H, however a quadplane with motors mounted on booms secured to the wings would normally be setup as an X frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:270
#: 331698f8e39e490eb8204d851ec02cd0
msgid "Step 9: Notch Filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:272
#: b239acf4830e42ca91b2ffb6bdc9fc77
msgid "After your have QHOVER flying without oscillations the next step is to get get a good notch filter setup to reduce noise to the VTOL PID controllers. A good set of notch filtering parameters is critical to a good tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:277
#: ea8ee22617e14aa2b176455d988335e7
msgid "To get a notch filter setup you need to hover your QuadPlane for 2 minutes with no pilot input and with :ref:`INS_LOG_BAT_MASK <INS_LOG_BAT_MASK>` set to 1. This will enable FFT logging which will guide the correct setup of the notch filters. You should then carefully read the :ref:`common-imu-notch-filtering` documentation and setup a harmonic notch to remove the noise from your gyros."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:284
#: 8751bd465b2a4aa18f75988a32c871c2
msgid "When setting up your filtering you should consider the cause of any oscillation you find. On most aircraft the vibrations you find will be directly caused by a multiple of the RPM, but on some aircraft a frame resonance or resonance in the autopilot mount may be the cause. Understanding the cause of any resonances is critical to reducing noise enough to get a good tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:292
#: 462086d44ff7410789663535ed3c5053
msgid "Step 10: Manual tuning of Roll and Pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:294
#: bcd7039ef3174951ab763de5f7c45122
msgid "While you may be tempted to jump straight to autotuning, this is not recommended. Most QuadPlanes need some manual tuning of roll and pitch before they can handle an autotune. If you jump straight to an autotune then your aircraft may become unstable enough to crash. A good manual tune will also reduce the amount of time an autotune will take, which can be critical given the small VTOL hover times of many QuadPlanes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:302
#: d8d7c734933c48a3aa8dc930554a244b
msgid "Before starting the manual tune you should go back and check you have fully completed the steps above, and ensure you have a good notch filter setup to remove noise from the gyros."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:306
#: ca3a4b85d8d849c397f076fcbe642691
msgid "Hover the aircraft in QSTABILIZE or QHOVER modes, in low wind, with good sky view and good GPS lock. You should adjust the rate gains as described below, using small \"twitches\" on the sticks after each change to try to trigger oscillation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:311
#: 8cbecc0aca134631b147ac5d6fe47467
msgid "If oscillations start do not make large or sudden stick inputs. Reduce the throttle smoothly to land the aircraft while using very slow and small roll and pitch inputs to control the aircraft position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:315
#: 4313dd68e6a64e4582248f0e6b8b5ee8
msgid "The parameters you will be adjusting are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:318
#: a4bf792a048b4dbb8cad9f21dcef825c
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_P <Q_A_RAT_RLL_P>` and :ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_I <Q_A_RAT_RLL_I>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:320
#: 8a9d5ff56bf748d9abdc52c66ceb1d87
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_P <Q_A_RAT_PIT_P>` and :ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_I <Q_A_RAT_PIT_I>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:322
#: e4a71e35642f4e82bbdea2b53426f9ae
msgid "If the VTOL motors do not tilt, then the ``Q_A_RAT_PIT_FF`` and  ``Q_A_RAT_YAW_FF`` will be zero and corrections are dominated by P/I/D. But if pitch or yaw control is primarily by tilting the motors, then the FF terms dominate and P/D are primarily for disturbance correction. For tuning a tilted motor controlled axis, see :ref:`pitch-yaw-tuning`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:324
#: b2241425dd85459daac37c42af78d3bd
msgid "Start with the roll parameters, then move onto the pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:326
#: 69d2dce5124c476b86e3bacd1e210765
msgid "Increase the D term in steps of 50% until oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:327
#: c5ac28c1286e4ababa247036aa8cf6fc
msgid "Reduce the D term in steps of 10% until the oscillation disappears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:328
#: 70b12cec55dc4397b7bd68ab7de411a8
msgid "Reduce the D term by a further 25%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:329
#: 031a91087f10453fb32dc8916bad566e
msgid "Increase the P term in steps of 50% until oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:330
#: 183899b500cb459ea3b3433454cd556a
msgid "Reduce the P term in steps of 10% until the oscillation disappears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:331
#: f10bce7e514c43cca4ee5344cdaf3121
msgid "Reduce the P term by a further 25%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:333
#: b06c32b5a7f4497e985c298ba821cf0d
msgid "Each time the P term is changed in the above steps you should set the corresponding I term equal to the P term. Those parameters can be changed on ground and preferably disarmed. Alternatively, a confident pilot could set them in flight with a GCS, or use the transmitter tuning option. See :ref:`common-transmitter-tuning`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:339
#: a6ff9d17fa674c699200d458a4368914
msgid "Note that it is common that once you have properly setup notch filtering that you will be able to increase the D value a lot from the default value. Increases of 10x over the default are not uncommon. Being able to use a larger D gain is one of the main advantages of good notch filtering, and can produce a much better tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:346
#: 19071ee573af45a2bf1860b74c02d69d
msgid "After you have gone through the above steps you should carefully look at your logs to ensure you don't have a hidden oscillation. The structure of QuadPlanes sometimes means that oscillations may not be externally visible. You should use the RATE, PIQR and PIQP messages to look for oscillations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:353
#: d7bcab7b31fe4655a92deb55c81aaf23
msgid "Step 11: Evaluating the aircraft tune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:355
#: 80d353c0315f450c8b567f3d8b6ef134
msgid "You need to evaluate the aircraft's tune to see if the previous steps have resulted in a tune which is good enough for a transition flight or for autotuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:359
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:370
#: 1c89339e3c34456e9a007bf9bc3d4136
#: f591f31688ab4a5fbb8187cd7e73209a
msgid "Take off in QHOVER or QSTABILIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:360
#: e0e3e73fa6da495fb4f249a1a73cb864
msgid "Apply small roll and pitch inputs. Start with 5 degree inputs and releasing the stick to centre, pitch, left, right, roll forward back, then all 4 points on the diagonal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:361
#: daf8f35b0f4f4000afc27edfe6521e80
msgid "Increase inputs gradually to full stick deflection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:362
#: 62045eaee1f342d58eca0b630906ff31
msgid "Go to full stick deflection, quickly momentarily, and let the sticks spring back to centre"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:364
#: a55656a32c674831aa4520234ac7c8b0
msgid "If the aircraft begins to overshoot significantly or oscillate after the stick input, halt the tests before the situation begins to endanger the aircraft. The aircraft may require more manual tuning before autotuning can be run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:368
#: 9af71888ece64100a9eb5c33d01e3d82
msgid "To test the stabilization loops independent of the input shaping, set the parameter: :ref:`Q_A_RATE_FF_ENAB <Q_A_RATE_FF_ENAB>` to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:371
#: 02d558af01874acbad596e7b966cddba
msgid "Hold a roll or pitch input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:372
#: 837aa2d97527421694b7a245e8d3666e
msgid "Release the stick and observe the overshoot as the aircraft levels itself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:373
#: e26605c3278d4d48b000d1d7db2cc035
msgid "Gradually increase the stick deflection to 100%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:375
#: cc87dbd489de4bfb8a7de899f83f459c
msgid "Halt the tests if the aircraft overshoots level significantly or if the aircraft oscillates and go back to manual tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:378
#: cbd2f6ca4c3e44c5a06a1b6d8654bf11
msgid "Set :ref:`Q_A_RATE_FF_ENAB <Q_A_RATE_FF_ENAB>` to 1 after the tests are complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:381
#: c61f3876ad524dbbb00223a34453da0d
msgid "Step 12: Autotuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:382
#: 3f3d01ab6c084bb797df4a21ed2bd306
msgid "Often, the default params or a good manual tune will be sufficient. However, autotuning can usually improve the tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:384
#: 4f33fb57b7534b03b300b1aecfaa663d
msgid "If the aircraft appears stable enough to attempt autotuning and you have sufficient battery to last through an autotuning session then you can autotune using one of two methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:387
#: 21636e669e76465491bf3134f977f505
msgid ":ref:`QUICKTUNE <quicktune>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:388
#: 4dc10481661440bd90edeeab0f4567f5
msgid "QAUTOTUNE Mode (no longer the recommended method, and is not compiled into most firmware)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:391
#: 1dc92bc714d24113a31c00ba62cf4bdb
msgid "Using the Quick VTOL Tune LUA Applet to Automate Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:392
#: de034146c6994c0284f16f835d9bde5f
msgid "As of ArduPlane 4.6, this is now integrated into the firmware as code, directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:394
#: bb621a586d264b18961876bfa0a7f2d0
msgid "For systems using an autopilot with sufficient memory to run :ref:`LUA scripts <common-lua-scripts>`, such as F7 and H7 based controllers, this process has been automated via a LUA Applet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:396
#: 34ad12bf93164338b1bbece03a57cc47
msgid "Be sure that scripting has been setup and sufficient memory has been allocated, as explained in :ref:`LUA scripts <common-lua-scripts>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:398
#: fc6acf5d060048acb8482e066b7668c4
msgid "See the `Quick VTOL Tune LUA script <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/VTOL-quicktune.md>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:402
#: 7abe2c1d1f634a8a9c19bc3c07b9a50c
msgid "Using the QAUTOTUNE mode to Automate Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:404
#: 9d5adbeea5c9479b9c6d73c402e7220c
msgid "Follow the instructions in the :ref:`QAUTOTUNE<qautotune-mode>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:406
#: ecf8da2b84af4c2788d25076de81d093
msgid "You should use QAUTOTUNE on one axis at a time (setting :ref:`Q_AUTOTUNE_AXES <Q_AUTOTUNE_AXES>` for the axis you want to tune). An autotune of a single axis will typically take 5 to 8 minutes, but will take longer if your manual tune is not good enough. If you do not have enough battery for at least 8 minutes of vertical flight then QAUTOTUNE is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:413
#: dfd5a074c5a140299bd894fe856c4be5
msgid "There a number of problems that can prevent QAUTOTUNE from providing a good tune. Some of the reason QAUTOTUNE can fail are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:415
#: 500bc33330114771b97579c40bfe421a
msgid "High levels of gyro noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:416
#: 95d1d1883a1644fda5d48816b898decb
msgid "Incorrect value of :ref:`Q_M_THST_EXPO <Q_M_THST_EXPO>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:417
#: 94d34ccb1c6d41a7999b35a8b3f062c4
msgid "Flexible frame or payload mount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:418
#: e3d4519cba664093ab610ca1859fcfce
msgid "Overly flexible vibration isolation mount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:419
#: 2e02dbb311d641fd8ebe11cf13bd219c
msgid "Non-linear ESC response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:420
#: 41c14b074ce44e65834a3859c689256e
msgid "Very low setting for :ref:`Q_M_SPIN_MIN <Q_M_SPIN_MIN>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:421
#: 11c841fc78c043299391215c29f9141e
msgid "Overloaded propellers or motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:422
#: 3ca9fa0997244324b656d0e3d867b69e
msgid "Autotuning a Tailsitter's pitch or yaw axis, or vectored yaw axis on TiltRotor, since they require feed-forward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:424
#: daf71dc702f74a74ad6658d08025d005
msgid "If QAUTOTUNE has failed you will need to re-do a manual tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:426
#: 131ea6cc4561439b98c2d874a632e82f
msgid "Some signs that QAUTOTUNE has been successful are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:428
#: db64253589684ea88aac7f98a4d15b42
msgid "An increase in the values of :ref:`Q_A_ANG_PIT_P <Q_A_ANG_PIT_P>` and :ref:`Q_A_ANG_RLL_P <Q_A_ANG_RLL_P>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:429
#: 797af88c10354c9fb532cb3d693fb1ad
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_D <Q_A_RAT_PIT_D>` and :ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_D <Q_A_RAT_RLL_D>` are larger than :ref:`Q_AUTOTUNE_MIN_D <Q_AUTOTUNE_MIN_D>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:431
#: 7df738d9fea74f7abdb906f947e4f77d
msgid "QAUTOTUNE will attempt to tune each axis as tight as the aircraft can tolerate. In some aircraft this can be unnecessarily responsive. A guide for most aircraft:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:433
#: 5a133a2dc1164969a26d0594eb377fa2
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_ANG_PIT_P <Q_A_ANG_PIT_P>` should be reduced from 10 to 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:434
#: 1c2eb0edd3954b65a299395ff5ea7f46
msgid ":ref:`Q_A_ANG_RLL_P <Q_A_ANG_RLL_P>` should be reduced from 10 to 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning-process.rst:435
#: 917b149290ba4853931a0b8a90a38bf4
